.ruff_cache/

# PyPI configuration file
.pypirc

# ── Run results (guide/05-archiving.md) ──────────────────────────────────────
# The blanket `*.log` rule above is right for the LIVE logs at the repo root —
# every run truncates those. It is wrong for the archive: results/<run-id>/ is
# one immutable run, it is what the notebook reads, and it is the deliverable.
!results/**/*.log

# Per-device scratch, not results (guide/05 §5): superseded by the pooled logs,
# and a leftover copy silently poisons the next run's numbers. Name the scratch
# files EXACTLY: `message_size_*.log` also matched the archived
# `results/<run>/message_size_series.log`, and a later rule beats the negation
# above — so every pushed archive lost half of an all-or-none family (01 §2)
# and the reader hard-failed on "emit both or neither".
metrics_raw_*.csv
metrics_pivoted*.csv
metrics_pivot.lock
timing_edge_*.log
timing_cloud_*.log
message_size_local.log

# Re-assert it last: an archived run is the deliverable, and no scratch rule
# added below may clip a file out of one.
!results/**/*.log

# Fabricated run used to exercise the validators and the notebook before real
# results exist (scratch/make_synthetic_run.py). Regenerable, and it must never
# be mistaken for a measurement.
scratch/synthetic/
